    "sections": {
        "changelog": "<h4>3.0.8</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: setting sanitization with defaults recovery</li>\n<li>feat: add wp rest mirror template</li>\n<li>feat: wp rest reuse authorization if exists</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>3.0.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: addons mount method</li>\n<li>feat: improve debug console outputs</li>\n<li>fix: exclude loco files from git</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "description": "<p>Bridge any backend or service data to posts collections.</p>\n<h3>How it works</h3>\n<p>Posts Bridge handles posts collections as indexes that represents your backend data and allows the use of Gutenberg, the powerful page builder of WordPress, as your backend frontend builder.</p>\n<h3>Addons</h3>\n<p>Posts Bridge has core support for REST API connexions and addons for <a href=\"https://www.odoo.com/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Odoo</a>, <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/rest-api/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">WordPress REST API</a> and <a href=\"https://workspace.google.com/products/sheets/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Google Spreadsheets</a>.</p>\n<h3>Docs</h3>\n<p>See the official plugin&#8217;s documentation on our <a href=\"https://git.coopdevs.org/codeccoop/wp/plugins/posts-bridge/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">gitlab repository</a>.</p>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Bridge any backend or service data to posts collections.",
